  <body>
    <main>
      <div class="container">
        <a class="back-link" href="/">← Back to portfolio</a>

        <h1>World Happiness Report Dashboard</h1>

        <p class="summary">
          Analysis of the World Happiness Report dataset combining Python ETL workflows with 
          interactive Power BI dashboards to explore global well-being indicators.
        </p>

        <p class="tools">Python · ETL · Power BI</p>

        <div class="hero-image">
          <img
            src="/projects/world-happiness-dashboard.jpg"
            alt="World Happiness Report Dashboard"
          />
        </div>

        <section class="section">
          <h2>Project Overview</h2>
          <p>
            This project explored the World Happiness Report dataset to better understand the social, economic, 
            and behavioral factors associated with well-being across countries. The work combined exploratory data analysis, 
            dataset transformation, and interactive visualization to examine how variables such as life satisfaction, 
            social support, and generosity relate to reported happiness levels.

            A key focus of the project was understanding the methodology behind the data itself. 
            This included reviewing official World Happiness Report and Gallup documentation to interpret 
            how variables were collected and defined, and how differences in survey methods or sample sizes might affect cross-country comparisons.

            The final output was an interactive Power BI dashboard that allows users to explore global trends, 
            compare continents, and drill down into individual country metrics.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <h2>What I Worked On</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Reviewed World Happiness Report and Gallup documentation to understand how key variables 
                such as Life Ladder, Generosity, and Social Support were collected and defined.</li>
            <li>Conducted exploratory data analysis to assess distributions, missing values, and potential reporting biases across countries.</li>
            <li>Developed reusable Python functions to automate data inspection tasks during EDA and ETL workflows.</li>
            <li>Collaborated on data cleaning and transformation pipelines using Python and Jupyter notebooks.</li>
            <li>Built the global map visualization and designed the country-level dashboard view in Power BI.</li>
            <li>Structured the dashboard narrative to move from global overview → continental comparison → country-level analysis.</li>
            <li>Served as Scrum Master, coordinating sprint progress and project milestones.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <h2>Key Highlights</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Interactive Power BI dashboard combining global, regional, and country-level views of happiness indicators.</li>
            <li>Integration of additional datasets to provide methodological context for the World Happiness data.</li>
            <li>Analysis of missing values and reporting differences across countries while preserving original data integrity (no imputation).</li>
            <li>Dashboard designed to guide users from macro global trends to micro country-level insights.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

